@startuml ML Predictions Workflow
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam activityBackgroundColor #ECF0F1
skinparam activityBorderColor #2C3E50
skinparam arrowColor #3498DB

title Machine Learning Traffic Congestion Prediction Workflow

skinparam sequence {
  ActorBackgroundColor #FFEFD5
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #E8F8F5
  DatabaseBackgroundColor #D4E6F1
}

actor User
participant "Frontend" as FE
participant "API Controller" as API
participant "ML Service" as ML
database "predictions.json" as PredDB

== Data Preparation Phase ==

note right of ML
  Training Data:
  - 722 records
  - Features: road_id, period, 
    historical_flow, time_of_day,
    day_of_week, weather
  - Target: congestion_level (0-2)
end note

note right of ML
  Model: Gradient Boosting
  - n_estimators: 100
  - max_depth: 6
  - learning_rate: 0.1
  - R² Score: 0.94
end note

== Prediction Phase ==

User -> FE : Enable "Use ML Predictions"
FE -> API : GET /api/ml-predictions?period=MORNING

alt With Time Period
    API -> ML : GetPredictions(period)
else Without Period
    API -> ML : GetAllPredictions()
end

ML -> PredDB : Load prediction data

alt Cache Available
    ML -> ML : Return cached predictions
else
    PredDB -->> ML : Load 722 prediction records
    ML -> ML : Apply model inference
end

ML --> API : List<MlPredictionDto>
API --> FE : { predictions: [...] }

note right of FE
  Display:
  - Roads colored by congestion
  - Red: >= 1.5 (high)
  - Orange: >= 1.0 (medium)
  - Yellow: >= 0.7 (low-medium)
  - Green: < 0.7 (low)
end note

== Integration with Time-Varying Dijkstra ==

User -> FE : Select "Time-Varying Route"
FE -> API : GET /api/route-planning/time-route?from=L1&to=L5&useMl=true

API -> ML : GetPredictions(period)
API -> ML : GetGraph()

loop For each edge in Dijkstra
    ML -> ML : Apply congestion weight
    note right of ML
      Weight = distance * (1 + congestion_factor * predicted_congestion)
    end note
end

API --> FE : Route with ML-optimized weights

@enduml